    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376">

                <pb facs="0491" n="379" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg379"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Dawson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-03-19"><hi rendition="#italic">March 19,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to your telegram received 18th and department’s reply of to-day. We
                    sincerely hope that any difficulty about defining the limits of Jurado will not
                    interfere with the ratification of the treaty. <pb facs="0492" n="380"
                        xml:id="pg380"/> There seems to be some difficulty here about the Panama
                    minister being willing to exchange notes, although I have not yet had an
                    opportunity to talk to him.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
